# =============================================================================
# .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# The rule behind every line here: commit what a fresh clone cannot regenerate.
# Code and inputs go in. Anything `Rscript run_all.R` rebuilds stays out.
# =============================================================================


## ---- Generated output -------------------------------------------------------
# 7.5 MB of the project's 7.9 MB lives here, and it is all derived from R/ + data/.
# Binary files (png/pdf/emf/xlsx) do not diff, so git stores a complete new copy on
# every rerun. Committing them means a repo that grows by ~7 MB each time you
# regenerate figures, in exchange for nothing you cannot rebuild in one command.
#
# When you need a fixed snapshot — a paper submission, a supervisor handover — force
# the specific files in and tag it, rather than tracking the whole tree:
#     git add -f output/tables/results.xlsx output/figures/final
#     git commit -m "Figures as submitted, 2026-08"
#     git tag submission-v1

output/


## ---- Data: raw and final are deliberately NOT ignored ------------------------
# Most R templates ignore data/ wholesale. Do not do that here.
#
#   data/raw/     CPI, gold, BCOM. Downloaded by hand, ~70 KB. If these are lost
#                 the project cannot be rebuilt at all.
#
#   data/final/   infl_macro.csv is the only surviving record of the 28-series FRED
#                 panel for a given pull date. Stage 1 fetches FRED live and never
#                 saves the untouched download, and FRED revises its history — so
#                 re-running stage 1 later produces different numbers. Until stage 1
#                 caches its raw pull to data/raw/, this file is your reproducibility
#                 anchor. Commit it.
#
#   data/temp/    rebuilt by stage 1 on every run, so it is ignored below.

data/temp/


## ---- R session artefacts ----------------------------------------------------
# .Rhistory in particular: it is a transcript of everything typed in the console,
# including paths and anything pasted while debugging. It has no place in a repo.
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history

# Rscript writes this whenever a script draws to a screen device with none open
# (the acf()/pacf() calls in stages 1, 3 and 4). Regenerated on every run.
Rplots.pdf
.RData
.RDataTmp
.Ruserdata
.Renviron
.Rproj.user/
*.Rcheck/
.httr-oauth


## ---- renv (when you add it) -------------------------------------------------
# Commit renv.lock — it is the version manifest and the whole point.
# Never commit the library itself; it is hundreds of MB of compiled packages.
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/cellar/
renv/staging/
renv/sandbox/
.Rprofile.bak


## ---- Docker (when you add it) -----------------------------------------------
# Commit the Dockerfile. Keep local overrides and build state out.
docker-compose.override.yml
.env


## ---- Editors ----------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~


## ---- OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
